 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Dhul-Qarnayn is the righteous 'ruler' actor only. Gog and Magog are never drawn: no actor stands for them; the people only point toward the pass, and their gloss is Al-Muyassar's 'two great nations of the children of Adam' with no arrow. barrier_build runs from 'bars of iron' to 'molten copper' (18:96). In c4 the event sits on the first word only so the barrier stands complete (no rebuild intended). 18:98 is calm: the ruler speaks, raises his hands in gratitude and lowers his head; the levelling on the promised day is never shown. Review fix: Dhul-Qarnayn is shown as a neutral labelled light (his status is uncertain), like al-Khidr."
 },
